From: Tabor SPE port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] dfa: keep the stray-backslash label valid before C23

The Debian warning patch places a declaration directly after this label.
Add an empty statement so GCC 8 can compile it under the existing dialect.
No parser behavior or warning policy changes. Local compatibility patch
against Debian grep 3.11-4; retains upstream GNU licensing.

--- a/lib/dfa.c
+++ b/lib/dfa.c
@@ -1559,6 +1559,6 @@
           if (!backslash)
             goto normal_char;
-        stray_backslash:
+        stray_backslash: ;
           char const *userevalwarn;
           userevalwarn = getenv ("DEB_GREP_ENABLE_STRAY_BACKSLASH_WARN");
           if ((dfa->syntax.dfaopts & DFA_STRAY_BACKSLASH_WARN) &&
